  "body": "### What is the expected enhancement?\n\nOur current implementation of the `FCIDump` parser runs into **serious** bottlenecks for larger systems. This is mostly due to the fact of how we are dealing with loading the permutational symmetries. Instead of tracking the index tuples which we encounter and later on populating the symmetric variations, we construct the full list of potential index tuples ahead of time, and then \"cross off\" the ones that we did indeed find. Considering that the index tuples scale as `N^4`, this is obviously horrendously expensive for large `N`.\r\n\r\nThis issue suggests that the implementation be revisited and improved as to remove said bottleneck :+1: ",
